    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear strategy centered on exploiting the soft matchup against Trey Gibson. Our premier plays are **Tyler Soderstrom** (69.25) and **Corbin Carroll** (67.82), who anchor the offense. **Tyler Soderstrom** benefits from a massive 10% park factor boost and a favorable right-handed platoon advantage, while **Corbin Carroll** remains a top-tier start despite facing a lefty, as his elite profile and spot in the #3 hole provide high-floor production that is difficult to fade. **Brice Turang** also earns a strong recommendation (61.57) due to his high-leverage spot in the lineup and a favorable matchup against the lower-tier arm of M. P\u00e9rez.\n\nWe are carefully monitoring the lower end of the order, where **Dalton Rushing** (60.87) and **Alex Freeland** (56.46) are currently projected based on assumed lineup spots against the highly hittable Trey Gibson. These two provide a distinct efficiency edge due to the 19% SP skill boost; however, their scores are tempered by bottom-of-the-order penalties and pending official lineups. On the bench, **Cole Young** (41.98) was the closest cut from the active roster. While his platoon splits against Suarez are intriguing, he ultimately lost out because his total efficiency score failed to clear the threshold set by the depth of our starters against more vulnerable pitching rotations. \n\nThe biggest risk to our output remains the volatility of the back-end lineup spots for **Henry Bolte** and **Kyle Karros**, both of whom are hovering near the marginal tier. While the park factors for both are favorable, their low-order placement limits their ceiling for counting stats. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Austin Riley** (45.54), whose matchup against Misiorowski is the toughest on our sheet; his score is dragged down significantly by the opposing pitcher's elite skill. Should the confirmed lineups shift, we are prepared to pivot to protect our game caps, particularly as we await news on the health status of **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Giancarlo Stanton**, who remain sidelined.",
